From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:19:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: net: nfc: st,st-nci: add the reference clock

Some boards feed the controller's reference clock from the SoC instead of
a crystal. On Google's Pixel 7 phones the ST54J takes it from a PMU clock
output pad, which must run while the controller is powered up. Allow one
optional clock.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/nfc/st,st-nci.yaml | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/nfc/st,st-nci.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/nfc/st,st-nci.yaml
index 061367be5..eb4ee5c91 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/nfc/st,st-nci.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/nfc/st,st-nci.yaml
@@ -23,6 +23,12 @@ properties:
   reset-gpios:
     description: Output GPIO pin used for resetting the controller
 
+  clocks:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description:
+      Reference clock, if the controller is not fed by its own crystal. It
+      is enabled while the controller is powered up.
+
   ese-present:
     type: boolean
     description: |
